From: ReadyNAS NG <readynasng@build>
Subject: [PATCH 12/27] tty: serial: add the Padre UART driver

The two UARTs of the IT3107 (ttyS0 at 0x6000_0070, ttyS1 at
0x6000_0060, console at 9600 baud on the ReadyNAS Duo v1), same
numbering as NETGEAR's 2.6.17 padre_serial.c: interrupt-driven receive,
polled transmit, console support.
---
 drivers/tty/serial/Kconfig      |  14 ++
 drivers/tty/serial/Makefile     |   1 +
 drivers/tty/serial/padre_uart.c | 348 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 363 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/tty/serial/padre_uart.c

diff --git a/drivers/tty/serial/Kconfig b/drivers/tty/serial/Kconfig
index 2b9c8b39d68f553d269627cc137a21cde4ba903c..bcc2abfd8627e932fd240fb8b9e706a8ff5d060b 100644
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/Kconfig
@@ -1099,6 +1099,20 @@ config SERIAL_BCM63XX_CONSOLE
 	  If you have enabled the serial port on the BCM63xx CPU
 	  you can make it the console by answering Y to this option.
 
+config SERIAL_PADRE
+	bool "Infrant IT3107 Padre UART (ReadyNAS Duo v1)"
